Package: network-manager-openvpn3
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 network-manager (>= 1.30),
 openvpn3 | openvpn3-client,
 dbus-system-bus-common,
Description: NetworkManager VPN plugin for OpenVPN 3 — service (dh-cargo)
 nm-openvpn3 is a NetworkManager VPN service plugin that drives the
 OpenVPN 3 Linux session manager over D-Bus, written in Rust on top
 of zbus and tokio.
 .
 This experimental package is built via dh-cargo against
 `librust-*-dev` packages from the Debian / Ubuntu archive rather than
 a vendored cargo tarball.  The runtime payload — service daemon,
 auth-dialog, .name discovery file, dbus policy — is identical to the
 canonical network-manager-openvpn3 package.

Package: network-manager-openvpn3-gnome
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 network-manager-openvpn3 (= ${binary:Version}),
 libgtk-4-1 (>= 4.10),
 libadwaita-1-0 (>= 1.4),
Recommends: network-manager-gnome
Description: NetworkManager VPN plugin for OpenVPN 3 — GNOME UI (dh-cargo)
 GUI integration for nm-openvpn3 built via dh-cargo against archive
 `librust-*-dev` packages.  Ships the libnm-vpn-plugin discovery hook,
 the GTK4 / libadwaita property editor, gettext catalogs, and the
 AppStream metainfo file.
